      "note": "french-manoir (c01) and norman-vernacular (c04) each carry this as a hard, numbered structural constraint. french-provincial-farmhouse's own text does not restate it as a numbered constraint — its constraints list covers orientation, roof pitch, wall thickness and shutters, not depth — so the single-pile claim for this member rests on its structural-bay logic (a beam/purlin span between masonry cross-walls, which is a depth-limiting mechanism) and the total absence of any double-pile precedent anywhere in its text, rather than on an explicit statement. Marked judgment for that reason."
